# Built programs.
#
# `wails build` and `go build` recreate all of these in seconds, and they are
# large enough that committing them would dominate the repository's history.
# The source assets they are built from - build/appicon.png and
# build/windows/icon.ico - are tracked; the binaries are not.
*.exe

# Wails' generated JavaScript bindings. Regenerated on every build, and this
# project has no npm step that would need them checked in.
frontend/wailsjs/

# The installer's payload, packed fresh on every build from build/bin, which
# is already ignored above.
cmd/godl-setup/payload/*.zip

# Go build and test artefacts.
*.test
*.out
*.prof
coverage.*

# Scratch space some of the verification scripts use.
*.part
*.log

# Editor and operating-system noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor and compiler backup files. `godl-host.exe~` slipped past the `*.exe`
# rule above and was committed once, which is why this line exists.
*~
